  "design": [
    "Huawei baseline starts its independent original Range immediately; usable selected stream needs no extra speed qualification.",
    "Non-baseline video qualifies its own current-media middle or seek-local256KiB body supply before owning a long-lived stream slot; scratch bytes are discarded and counted in the shared payload reservation.",
    "Qualified probe own total/ETag/Last-Modified must match the chosen full response. Weak fallback uses its own independent response; no probe bytes are appended.",
    "Measured inadequate body supply ranks behind unavailable or metadata-uncertain qualifications. Weak fallback4s/2.5s gates retain250ms per-candidate staggering and a6s overall initial race bound.",
    "Short explicit/suffix Range bypasses throughput ranking; unknown near-tail Range can use a one-byte reference without a throughput gate.",
    "Initial qualification avg-times2/1MiB floor is distinct from selected video continuous supply avg-times1.25/256KiB floor. Rolling supply only measures upstream waiting.",
    "Player flush/backpressure has no upstream timeout. One cancellation listener per response interrupts its current pending write; close/seek still destroy the socket.",
    "Original strict byte/total/version admission, bounded complete pair retry, ordered hedge, shared64MiB reservations, and post-slot origin watchdog are preserved."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "These are transport byte/timing fixtures, not real video decoding or graphical acceptance.",
    "Real authenticated Singapore media and native4MiB/16s-buffer performance validation are owned by the root run and must be reported separately.",
    "The max_gap metric includes initial response latency and deliberate consumer pauses; it is not a native cache-pause metric.",
    "A small qualification sample and bitrate-derived headroom do not prove cache hits, future VBR peak capacity, or global fastest CDN selection.",
    "diagnostics.selected_hosts only describes preferred/initial stream hosts per-media, not every chunk or candidate that participated.",
    "64MiB is the shared logical payload reservation budget, not an assertion about Dart process total heap or kernel TCP buffers; fixture peaks do not saturate this budget."
  ]
